Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: serialize group lifecycle and stop QMI before release

Carry the RC01 lifecycle delta from 1f23a593fcbf775a849c7cb9f3709f8a899d7c99
onto the regrouped upstream code. Preserve stable WSI device IDs and endpoint
checks. Initialize work at allocation, reject late events, stop work outside
group/core locks, and release memory under the group lock. Process lifecycle
serialization covers publication through removal; workers never take it.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -35,7 +35,12 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(ftm_mode, "Boots up in factory test mode");
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(ath12k_ftm_mode);
 
-/* protected with ath12k_hw_group_mutex */
+/* Process-context lifecycle lock, also protecting list membership/lifetime.
+ * Held from lookup/publication through create, and stop through last free.
+ * QMI/restart/reset workers must never acquire it: they only need ag->mutex,
+ * which is dropped before their work is cancelled. Lock order is this mutex
+ * -> ag->mutex -> core_lock. This serialises independent group init/remove.
+ */
 static struct list_head ath12k_hw_group_list = LIST_HEAD_INIT(ath12k_hw_group_list);
 
 static DEFINE_MUTEX(ath12k_hw_group_mutex);
@@ -873,6 +878,7 @@
 {
 	int ret;
 
+	lockdep_assert_held(&ab->ag->mutex);
 	if (ath12k_ftm_mode) {
